## Problem

When users created a new game lobby, the invite popup had two critical issues:
1. **Empty text field** - The popup would show but the invite link field was blank
2. **Non-functional copy button** - Clicking "Copy" wouldn't copy anything to clipboard

This made it impossible for users to easily share newly created games with friends.

## Root Cause

The issue was in the `copyLobbyLink` event handler in `main.js`. The code attempted to use the native `navigator.share` API first, and only showed the manual share modal as a fallback when native sharing failed. However, this logic had problems:

```javascript
// Problematic code
if (navigator.share) {
  navigator.share({ url }).catch(() => {
    // Only shows modal if native share fails
    shareLink.value = url;
    shareModal.style.display = 'flex';
    // ...
  });
}
```

Additionally, there was no automatic triggering of the invite popup after lobby creation.

## Solution

### 1. Fixed Share Link Population
Simplified the logic to always show the modal with the correct URL instead of trying native share first:

```javascript
// Fixed code - always shows modal
copyLobbyLink.addEventListener('click', () => {
  const url = window.location.href;
  shareLink.value = url;
  shareModal.style.display = 'flex';
  openDialog(shareModal);
  shareLink.focus();
  shareLink.select();
});
```

### 2. Added Auto-Show After Lobby Creation
Implemented a localStorage flag system to automatically display the invite popup for newly created lobbies:

```javascript
// In landing.js - set flag when lobby is created
localStorage.setItem('showInvitePopup', data.id);

// In main.js - check flag and auto-show
const showInviteFor = localStorage.getItem('showInvitePopup');
if (showInviteFor === LOBBY_CODE) {
  localStorage.removeItem('showInvitePopup');
  setTimeout(() => copyLobbyLink.click(), 1000);
}
```

### 3. Enhanced Copy Button
Added validation and better error handling for clipboard operations:

```javascript
if (!shareLink.value) {
  showMessage('No link to copy!', { messageEl, messagePopup });
  return;
}
navigator.clipboard.writeText(shareLink.value).then(() => {
  showMessage('Link copied!', { messageEl, messagePopup });
}).catch((err) => {
  showMessage('Failed to copy link. Try selecting and copying manually.', { messageEl, messagePopup });
});
```

### 4. Fixed Asset Serving
Resolved MIME type issues with Vite-generated assets by adding proper `/assets/` routes to the Flask server, preventing JavaScript files from being served as HTML.

## Testing Results ✅

All functionality has been verified through browser testing:

- ✅ **Auto-show**: Invite popup appears automatically after creating a new lobby
- ✅ **Correct URL**: Text field populates with proper lobby URL (`http://127.0.0.1:5001/lobby/ABC123`)  
- ✅ **Working copy**: Copy button successfully copies URL to clipboard with confirmation message
- ✅ **Manual trigger**: 🔗 button in lobby header also works correctly

## Screenshots

![Working invite popup](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3229871c-ace3-4023-9023-35bbaa84a5c7)

The screenshot shows the invite popup automatically displayed after lobby creation, with the correct URL populated in the text field and working copy functionality.

## Files Changed

- `frontend/static/js/main.js` - Fixed share link handler and added auto-show logic
- `frontend/landing.js` - Added lobby creation flag for auto-popup trigger  
- `backend/server.py` - Fixed asset serving routes for Vite-generated files

Users can now seamlessly create games and share them with friends using the fully functional invite popup system.

